  "scope": "Ordinary and audited cancellation plus retry settlement move under the existing product settlement module. Native journals keep authority and transactions; native owners retain cache publication, exact terminal retry copy order and visible group selection.",
  "limitations": [
    "Trusted composition after caller-owned admission. No raw ingress validation, authentication, lease authority or native durable recovery is granted by these adapters.",
    "A visible fault can follow a successful commit. Ordinary cancellation, audited cancellation and terminal retry retain their distinct return shapes without retries or compensation.",
    "Frozen coordinators share existing journal and group-visibility kernels. Native completion/maturity and complete extraction gates remain unchanged.",
    "Group visibility, cache reconciliation, journal ownership, complete host-neutral durable recovery, vertical compatibility and physical extraction remain open.",
    "Local macOS Rust/SQLite verification only; no Linux, GUI runtime or remote CI run, and no freshly exported standalone checkpoint."
  ],
